<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zwaanendael</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1631–1632</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Zwaanendael Colony</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zwaanendael was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> whaling and farming settlement founded in 1631 near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lewes-delaware">Lewes, Delaware</a>, by patroons of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company">Dutch West India Company</a>. Within about a year a quarrel with the local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lenape">Lenape</a> led to its destruction and the killing of all its settlers. Though short-lived, it gave the Dutch a claim to the Delaware valley, and Delaware dates its first European settlement to it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zwaanendael.jpg" alt="Zwaanendael" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johannes Vingboons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Delaware_Bay_Vinckeboons_14.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
